# Phase 28 probe — run once, deliberately, under the refetch protocol
# (not part of the normal offline pipeline; network-touching).
#
# Purpose (Q4): discover the SHAPE of Camera group-membership ("adesione")
# interval data before writing any importer. The v2 deputies query
# (tools/queries/camera_deputati.rq) proves an adesione carries
# `ocd:endDate` (it MINUS-es adesioni that have one, to keep only the
# currently-open membership) and links a group via
# `ocd:rif_gruppoParlamentare` — but the START-date predicate and the full
# predicate vocabulary of an `ocd:aderisce` resource are NEVER SELECT-ed by
# that query, so they are unknown and must be verified here, not assumed.
#
# This is step 1 of the exploration: a plain SELECT DISTINCT over every
# predicate present on any XIX deputato's adesione resources. Aggregate-free
# (dati.senato.it rejects GROUP BY/COUNT with 403/400 — Phase 15b — and the
# Camera votes work deliberately never leaned on aggregates either, Phase 27
# Q3; so probes stay on plain SELECT/SELECT DISTINCT on both endpoints).
# The result is the predicate list that a step-2 full dump then materializes
# into concrete (start, end, group) columns for the byte projection and the
# group-switcher/reconciliation checks.
#
# Endpoint: https://dati.camera.it/sparql   License: CC BY 4.0
PREFIX ocd: <http://dati.camera.it/ocd/>

SELECT DISTINCT ?p
WHERE {
  ?d a ocd:deputato ;
     ocd:rif_leg <http://dati.camera.it/ocd/legislatura.rdf/repubblica_19> ;
     ocd:aderisce ?aderisce .
  ?aderisce ?p ?o .
}
ORDER BY ?p
